# Dependencies
# ⚠ NO TRAILING SLASH, DELIBERATELY. `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY and NOT
# a SYMLINK of the same name, so a lane that symlinks an installed tree between
# clones (a normal thing to do when running several worktrees) has that symlink
# picked up by `git add -A` and COMMITTED as mode 120000.
#
# It then fails only in CI, which is the worst place for it: the real install
# replaces the symlink with a directory, `git status` reports ` D node_modules`,
# and the Production Build guard fails on "a build must not dirty the tree".
# Locally the build stays clean, because locally the symlink IS what the tree has.
#
# Measured on this repo: with the slash, `git status` reports `?? node_modules`
# for a symlink; without it, the symlink is ignored and a real directory is still
# ignored. It happened twice in one session before this line was written.
node_modules

# Build outputs
dist/

